(6693468, 1001153, 134859, '<td valign="top">I loved the book and movie!  <br/>With regards to your photo, I think it is beautifully shot.  The softness of the picture makes it more inviting, I love the child to the right of the photo, it is a great addition (though when I first looked at the picture, the child is not what I noticed).  Then again, the child shouldn''t have been the center of attention, so it works well together.  I like the sepia choice as well.  It all flows well.  8</td>', 'I loved the book and movie!  With regards to your photo, I think it is beautifully shot.  The softness of the picture makes it more inviting, I love the child to the right of the photo, it is a great addition (though when I first looked at the picture, the child is not what I noticed).  Then again, the child shouldn''t have been the center of attention, so it works well together.  I like the sepia choice as well.  It all flows well.  8', '2012-02-27 14:28:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6693470, 1000827, 134859, '<td valign="top">Not sure which movie you are going after, there are two I know of titled "Unknown" but I never really watched them.  I think it''s a nice picture, there could have been some skin smoothing, or a warmer tone.  Maybe even a black and white conversion.  I think the natural light makes for harsh tones on the model''s face.  Just my personal opinion, however.</td>', 'Not sure which movie you are going after, there are two I know of titled "Unknown" but I never really watched them.  I think it''s a nice picture, there could have been some skin smoothing, or a warmer tone.  Maybe even a black and white conversion.  I think the natural light makes for harsh tones on the model''s face.  Just my personal opinion, however.', '2012-02-27 14:32:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6693471, 1001113, 134859, '<td valign="top">It''s an interesting picture.  I love the graininess here.  I also love that you didn''t choose the typical "hot girl slightly dressed" approach.  The wine glass with the whiskey (i''m assuming it''s whiskey) doesn''t exactly make sense, but then again, it''s all up for interpretation.</td>', 'It''s an interesting picture.  I love the graininess here.  I also love that you didn''t choose the typical "hot girl slightly dressed" approach.  The wine glass with the whiskey (i''m assuming it''s whiskey) doesn''t exactly make sense, but then again, it''s all up for interpretation.', '2012-02-27 14:34:27.000000', NULL, 1),
